1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:06,768
My doctor swore I had severe insomnia, but my alarm clock proves I have been dead for six hours.

2
00:00:07,068 --> 00:00:15,900
Every single night at midnight, my body freezes solid while my mind screams inside a cage of total darkness.

3
00:00:16,200 --> 00:00:23,592
Last night, I fought the paralysis. I managed to drag my frozen hand across the cold wooden floorboards.

4
00:00:23,892 --> 00:00:31,548
My fingers touched a glowing fiber-optic cable snaking out from beneath my heavy bedroom radiator.

5
00:00:31,848 --> 00:00:40,248
I yanked it hard. A digital meter on the wall instantly lit up with numbers ticking upward like a casino jackpot.

6
00:00:40,548 --> 00:00:50,460
A cold robotic voice whispered from the darkness, warning me that my unauthorized disconnection would trigger immediate termination.

7
00:00:50,760 --> 00:00:58,368
Termination of what? My lease? My job? Or the contract I apparently signed the day I was born?

8
00:00:58,668 --> 00:01:08,220
The screen showed my resting brainwaves powering high-frequency stock trading algorithms while my physical body rotted in bed.

9
00:01:08,520 --> 00:01:14,424
I am not an employee. I am a living battery pack leased out to Wall Street by my own hospital.

10
00:01:14,724 --> 00:01:20,220
My eyes are finally wide open. But tell me, who is sleeping in your bed right now?
